{
  "cells": [
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "# Multilingual NLP Notebook\n\n> Hands-on Build It and Exercises."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "## Build It"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 1: zero-shot cross-lingual classification"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "from transformers import AutoTokenizer, AutoModelForSequenceClassification"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "import torch"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "tok = AutoTokenizer.from_pretrained(\"joeddav/xlm-roberta-large-xnli\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "model = AutoModelForSequenceClassification.from_pretrained(\"joeddav/xlm-roberta-large-xnli\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        ""
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def classify(text, candidate_labels, hypothesis_template=\"This text is about {}.\"):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    scores = {}"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    for label in candidate_labels:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        hypothesis = hypothesis_template.format(label)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        inputs = tok(text, hypothesis, return_tensors=\"pt\", truncation=True)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        with torch.no_grad():"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            logits = model(**inputs).logits[0]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        entail_score = torch.softmax(logits, dim=-1)[2].item()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        scores[label] = entail_score"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    return dict(sorted(scores.items(), key=lambda x: -x[1]))"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        ""
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "print(classify(\"I love this product!\", [\"positive\", \"negative\", \"neutral\"]))"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "print(classify(\"\u092e\u0941\u091d\u0947 \u092f\u0939 \u0909\u0924\u094d\u092a\u093e\u0926 \u092a\u0938\u0902\u0926 \u0939\u0948!\", [\"positive\", \"negative\", \"neutral\"]))"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "print(classify(\"J'adore ce produit !\", [\"positive\", \"negative\", \"neutral\"]))"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "One model, three languages, same API. XLM-R trained on NLI data transfers well to classification via the entailment trick."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 2: multilingual embedding space"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "from sentence_transformers import SentenceTransformer"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "import numpy as np"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "model = SentenceTransformer(\"sentence-transformers/paraphrase-multilingual-MiniLM-L12-v2\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "pairs = ["
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    (\"The cat is sleeping.\", \"Le chat dort.\"),"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    (\"The cat is sleeping.\", \"El gato est\u00e1 durmiendo.\"),"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    (\"The cat is sleeping.\", \"Die Katze schl\u00e4ft.\"),"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    (\"The cat is sleeping.\", \"The dog is barking.\"),"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "for eng, other in pairs:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    emb_eng = model.encode([eng], normalize_embeddings=True)[0]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    emb_other = model.encode([other], normalize_embeddings=True)[0]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    sim = float(np.dot(emb_eng, emb_other))"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    print(f\"  {eng!r} <-> {other!r}: cos={sim:.3f}\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Translations land close in embedding space. A different English sentence lands further. This is what makes cross-lingual retrieval, clustering, and similarity work."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 3: few-shot fine-tuning strategy"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "from transformers import TrainingArguments, Trainer"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "from datasets import Dataset"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        ""
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def few_shot_finetune(base_model, base_tokenizer, examples):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    ds = Dataset.from_list(examples)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    def tokenize_fn(ex):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        out = base_tokenizer(ex[\"text\"], truncation=True, max_length=128)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        out[\"labels\"] = ex[\"label\"]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        return out"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    ds = ds.map(tokenize_fn)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    args = TrainingArguments("
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        output_dir=\"out\","
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        per_device_train_batch_size=8,"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        num_train_epochs=5,"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        learning_rate=2e-5,"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        save_strategy=\"no\","
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    )"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    trainer = Trainer(model=base_model, args=args, train_dataset=ds)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    trainer.train()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    return base_model"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "For 100-500 target-language examples, `num_train_epochs=5` and `learning_rate=2e-5` are the safe defaults. Higher learning rates cause the multilingual alignment to collapse and you get an English-only model."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "## Exercises"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "1. **Easy.** Run the zero-shot classification pipeline on 10 sentences per language across English, French, Hindi, and Arabic. Report accuracy on each. You should see strong French, decent Hindi, variable Arabic.\n2. **Medium.** Use `paraphrase-multilingual-MiniLM-L12-v2` to build a cross-lingual retriever over a small mixed-language corpus. Query in English, retrieve documents in any language. Measure recall@5.\n3. **Hard.** Compare English-source and Hindi-source fine-tuning for a Hindi classification task. Use 500 target-language examples for few-shot fine-tuning under both regimes. Report which source produces better Hindi accuracy and by how much. This is the LANGRANK thesis in miniature."
      ]
    }
  ],
